-- title:
--   Identity-weighted Lipschitz-gradient relaxation
-- statement:
--   For a probability measure `ν` on a finite-dimensional, second-countable normed inner-product space $V$, and a Haar measure `m` with $(ν : 	ext{Measure }V) \\ll m$, `Energy.LipschitzGradient.relaxation` is the sequential relaxation on $L^2(ν)$ of the squared gradient energy for globally Lipschitz tests. It is defined using the weighted-gradient operator with the identity map as weight; this bundle only defines the functional and does not assert any Poincaré inequality or finiteness property.
